<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Siaya Nuclear FPIC Campaign — proposal template</title><!--[if gte mso 9]><xml><w:WordDocument><w:View>Print</w:View><w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom></w:WordDocument></xml><![endif]--><style>body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4}h1{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:20pt;color:#0E3B2A;margin:4pt 0}h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:14pt;color:#0E3B2A;border-bottom:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding-bottom:2pt;margin:18pt 0 6pt}h3{font-size:11.5pt;color:#1B6B4A;margin:10pt 0 4pt}.kick{font-size:8.5pt;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#A34612;margin:0}.sub{color:#555;margin:0 0 8pt}.g{color:#7a7a7a;font-style:italic;font-size:10pt}.f{color:#999}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:6pt 0}th,td{border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;text-align:left}th{background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A}</style></head><body><p class="kick">MazingiraKenya · Je, Hatua? proposal kit · Collective / consortium template</p><h1>Siaya Nuclear FPIC Campaign</h1><p class="sub">Siaya · Nuclear · Challenge lane</p><p class="g">How to use: grey italic text is guidance — replace or delete it. Pre-filled text comes from the MazingiraKenya portfolio; rewrite it in your own voice and check every figure against the sources in the References section. If the funder has its own form, copy sections across.</p><h2>Cover sheet</h2><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Item</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Details</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Project title</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Siaya Nuclear FPIC Campaign</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Lead applicant (organisation)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Registration no. / legal status</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Contact person, email, phone</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Co-applicants / consortium members</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Location (counties / sub-counties)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Siaya</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Sector / theme</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Nuclear</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Duration</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">12 months</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Amount requested</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">KES 4.5M (indicative — confirm)</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Total project cost / co-funding</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Funder &amp; call reference</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h2>1. Executive summary</h2><p class="g">Half a page. Who you are (as a consortium), the problem, what you will do, for whom, the change you expect and the amount requested. Write this last.</p><p>Support Luanda Kotieno lake communities to secure free, prior and informed consent on the proposed nuclear plant. They are already protesting — without legal backing. Legal partner: Katiba Institute.</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><h2>2. The consortium</h2><p class="g">Introduce the lead applicant and each member. Funders want to see why this group, and why together — what each partner brings that others don&#39;t.</p><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Organisation</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Type / registration</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Base (county)</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Role in this project</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Relevant track record</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Lead: </td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Member: </td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Member: </td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h3>Why this partnership</h3><p class="g">How the members complement each other (e.g. community presence + legal expertise + research). History of working together, if any.</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><h3>Potential partners identified in the portfolio</h3><ul><li><b>Katiba Institute</b> — Lead legal partner: constitutional and participation litigation</li><li><b>Kenya Anti-Nuclear Alliance (KANA)</b> — Community alliance from the Kilifi campaign</li><li><b>Greenpeace Africa</b> — Campaign support and communication</li><li><b>SAFCEI</b> — Regional anti-nuclear and just-energy-transition ally</li></ul><p class="g">Confirm each partner&#39;s interest and role directly before naming them in a submission.</p><h2>3. Problem statement and evidence</h2><p class="g">Describe the problem, who is affected, why now, and what is missing. Cite sources (see References).</p><p>Kenya&#39;s Nuclear Power and Energy Agency (NuPEA) has moved its proposed first nuclear power plant from Uyombo in Kilifi to the Lake Victoria shore in Siaya County; reports point to the Luanda Kotieno / Sakwa area of Bondo Sub-County. Mongabay reports a 1,000 MW plant estimated at US$3.8 billion; NuPEA targets construction from 2027 and grid connection by 2034. Residents disrupted a public-participation forum in Sakwa in May 2026, after which NuPEA&#39;s CEO said nothing would be built without broad, informed community consent. The Luo Council of Elders rejected the project in December 2025, and in July 2026 a sensitisation meeting at Lenya, Central Sakwa ended in gunfire and arrests, according to the Kenya Anti-Nuclear Alliance. An independent review requested by NEMA reportedly found NuPEA&#39;s Strategic Environmental and Social Assessment fell short of IAEA good practice. Siting is still open — now is the time to secure real free, prior and informed consent.</p><p><b>The gap this project closes:</b> Siaya nuclear: proposed on Lake Victoria, community opposition with no legal support.</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><h2>4. Goal, objectives and theory of change</h2><p><b>Overall goal:</b></p><p class="g">One sentence on the long-term change you contribute to.</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><p><b>Specific objectives:</b></p><ol><li>Hold NuPEA to its public commitment that no plant is built without broad, informed community consent</li><li>Give Siaya communities independent, accessible information on siting, safety, water use and waste</li><li>Document participation failures and rights violations as a legal record</li><li>Secure a lawful, transparent site-selection and SESA/ESIA process</li></ol><p><b>Theory of change:</b></p><p class="g">IF we do [activities], THEN [outputs], WHICH LEADS TO [outcomes], BECAUSE [assumptions]. State the key assumptions.</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><h2>5. Activities and workplan</h2><p class="g">List activities under each objective. Mark the quarter(s) each happens in. Add the responsible partner.</p><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">#</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Activity</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Lead partner</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Q1</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Q2</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Q3</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Q4</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">1</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Run village-level FPIC and legal-literacy dialogues in Sakwa, Luanda Kotieno and nearby lakeshore communities (FAO FPIC manual)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">2</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Request the final SESA, site-selection reports and the independent review via ATI requests</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">3</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Commission plain-language expert review of siting, cooling-water and Lake Victoria impacts</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">4</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Monitor NuPEA forums and keep a rights-violations log with affidavits</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">5</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Obtain Katiba Institute legal opinion and prepare a possible petition, drawing on Ngolo v NuPEA (Kilifi)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">6</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Convene a community assembly to agree a community FPIC protocol for NuPEA and Siaya County</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h2>6. Division of labour</h2><p class="g">Who leads (L) and who supports (S) each workstream. Every activity needs exactly one lead.</p><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Workstream / activity</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Lead applicant</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Member 2</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Member 3</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Run village-level FPIC and legal-literacy dialogues in Sakwa, Luanda Kotieno and nearby lakeshore communities (FAO FPIC manual)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Request the final SESA, site-selection reports and the independent review via ATI requests</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Commission plain-language expert review of siting, cooling-water and Lake Victoria impacts</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Monitor NuPEA forums and keep a rights-violations log with affidavits</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Obtain Katiba Institute legal opinion and prepare a possible petition, drawing on Ngolo v NuPEA (Kilifi)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Convene a community assembly to agree a community FPIC protocol for NuPEA and Siaya County</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h2>7. Governance and decision-making</h2><p class="g">Describe the steering committee (who sits on it, how often it meets), how decisions are made (consensus / majority), how funds flow from lead to members, reporting deadlines between partners, and how disputes are resolved. Reference the signed MoU or consortium agreement (attach as annex).</p><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Mechanism</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Details</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Steering committee members &amp; frequency</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Decision rule</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Fund flow &amp; disbursement schedule</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Internal reporting deadlines</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Conflict resolution</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Communications &amp; attribution (logos, spokespeople)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Data ownership &amp; sharing between partners</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h2>8. Expected results and indicators (logframe)</h2><p class="g">One row per outcome. Indicators should be measurable; give a baseline and a target, and say how you&#39;ll verify.</p><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Result</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Indicator</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Baseline</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Target</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Means of verification</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">A community-endorsed FPIC protocol formally submitted to NuPEA and Siaya County</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Key SESA and site documents public, with an independent critique on record</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">An evidence base ready for legal action if consent standards are breached</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Output: </td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h2>9. Community participation, consent and safeguarding</h2><p class="g">How affected communities shape and lead the work; how you obtain free, prior and informed consent for testimony, photos, video and mapping; how you protect monitors, witnesses and defenders from retaliation; and how personal data is stored and shared in line with Kenya&#39;s Data Protection Act 2019. Attach your safeguarding and data-protection policies.</p><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Area</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Our approach</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Community leadership &amp; feedback</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Informed consent (FPIC) for documentation</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Security of monitors / witnesses</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Data protection (KDPA 2019)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Gender &amp; inclusion (women, youth, PWDs)</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Complaints / grievance mechanism</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h2>10. Legal and policy framework</h2><p class="g">Show how the project uses or enforces existing law. Pre-filled hooks below — keep those that apply.</p><ul><li>Constitution of Kenya 2010, Arts. 10, 35, 42, 69, 70</li><li>Nuclear Regulatory Act 2019 — licensing and siting of nuclear installations</li><li>EMCA 1999 and EIA/SEA regulations</li><li>FPIC standards: IFC Performance Standard 7 and UNDRIP; Fair Administrative Action Act 2015</li></ul><h2>11. Risks and mitigation</h2><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Risk</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Likelihood (L/M/H)</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Impact (L/M/H)</th><th style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;background:#E6F2EC;color:#0E3B2A;text-align:left">Mitigation</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Threats or intimidation against monitors/community members</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Access to information requests ignored or delayed</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Political or legal developments change the timeline</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Data loss or breach of sensitive testimony</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Partner withdraws or under-delivers</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><h2>12. Monitoring, evaluation and learning</h2><p class="g">How you will track progress (data, frequency, who), how communities take part in reviewing results, and how you&#39;ll share learning across the consortium. Mention any mid-term or final review.</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><h2>13. Budget summary</h2><p class="g