r:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Security &amp; safeguarding</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">Indirect / administrative costs</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">TOTAL</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #9DBFAE;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><p class="g">Explain sub-granting arrangements: how the lead transfers funds, financial reporting from members, and audit requirements.</p><h2>14. Sustainability and exit</h2><p class="g">What continues after the grant: skills, structures, data, relationships, follow-on funding (e.g. county climate funds under FLLoCA). Who owns the data and evidence afterwards?</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><p class="f">[ ]</p><h2>15. Annexes checklist</h2><ul><li>☐ Certificate of registration</li><li>☐ KRA PIN / tax compliance</li><li>☐ Latest audited accounts (or financial statements)</li><li>☐ Board / governance list</li><li>☐ Safeguarding policy</li><li>☐ Data protection policy</li><li>☐ CVs of key staff</li><li>☐ Letters of support from communities or partners</li><li>☐ Signed consortium agreement / MoU</li><li>☐ Letters of commitment from each member</li><li>☐ Each member&#39;s registration documents</li></ul><h2>16. References and supporting evidence</h2><ol><li>Africa&#39;s largest freshwater lake could be site of Kenya&#39;s nuclear power plant — Mongabay (Oct 2025). <a href="https://news.mongabay.com/2025/10/africas-largest-freshwater-lake-could-be-site-of-kenyas-nuclear-power-plant/">https://news.mongabay.com/2025/10/africas-largest-freshwater-lake-could-be-site-of-kenyas-nuclear-power-plant/</a></li><li>Siaya residents reject Kenya&#39;s nuclear plant at public forum — Greenpeace Africa (May 2026). <a href="https://www.greenpeace.org/africa/en/blog/60749/siaya-residents-reject-kenyas-nuclear-plant-at-public-forum-and-the-government-must-listen/">https://www.greenpeace.org/africa/en/blog/60749/siaya-residents-reject-kenyas-nuclear-plant-at-public-forum-and-the-government-must-listen/</a></li><li>NuPEA: No nuclear project without community consent — The Star (May 2026). <a href="https://www.the-star.co.ke/news/2026-05-23-nupea-no-nuclear-project-without-community-consent">https://www.the-star.co.ke/news/2026-05-23-nupea-no-nuclear-project-without-community-consent</a></li><li>KANA condemns violence against communities in Siaya — SAFCEI / KANA (Jul 2026). <a href="https://safcei.org/press-release-kana-condemns-violence-against-communities-in-siaya-and-calls-for-a-rights-based-just-energy-transition-in-kenya/">https://safcei.org/press-release-kana-condemns-violence-against-communities-in-siaya-and-calls-for-a-rights-based-just-energy-transition-in-kenya/</a></li><li>Ngolo &amp; another v NuPEA &amp; 2 others [2024] KEELC 14071 — ELC Malindi / Kenya Law. <a href="https://new.kenyalaw.org/akn/ke/judgment/keelc/2024/14071/eng@2024-12-19">https://new.kenyalaw.org/akn/ke/judgment/keelc/2024/14071/eng@2024-12-19</a></li><li>Nuclear Regulatory Act (Cap. 243) — Kenya Law. <a href="https://new.kenyalaw.org/akn/ke/act/2019/29">https://new.kenyalaw.org/akn/ke/act/2019/29</a></li><li>Free, Prior and Informed Consent: Manual for Project Practitioners — FAO (2016). <a href="https://www.fao.org/3/I6190E/i6190e.pdf">https://www.fao.org/3/I6190E/i6190e.pdf</a></li></ol><h3>Proposal-writing guides</h3><ul><li>How to write a concept note (FundsforNGOs): <a href="https://www.fundsforngos.org/proposal-writing/how-to-write-a-concept-note/">https://www.fundsforngos.org/proposal-writing/how-to-write-a-concept-note/</a></li><li>Logframe vs Theory of Change: what&#39;s the difference? (tools4dev): <a href="https://tools4dev.org/blog/logframe-vs-theory-of-change-whats-the-difference/">https://tools4dev.org/blog/logframe-vs-theory-of-change-whats-the-difference/</a></li><li>Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) template (tools4dev): <a href="https://tools4dev.org/resources/memorandum-of-understanding-mou-template/">https://tools4dev.org/resources/memorandum-of-understanding-mou-template/</a></li><li>Free, Prior and Informed Consent: manual for project practitioners (FAO): <a href="https://www.fao.org/3/I6190E/i6190e.pdf">https://www.fao.org/3/I6190E/i6190e.pdf</a></li><li>Video as Evidence field guide (WITNESS): <a href="https://vae.witness.org/video-as-evidence-field-guide/">https://vae.witness.org/video-as-evidence-field-guide/</a></li><li>Data Protection Act, 2019 (Kenya) (ODPC Kenya): <a href="https://www.odpc.go.ke/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/TheDataProtectionAct__No24of2019.pdf">https://www.odpc.go.ke/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/TheDataProtectionAct__No24of2019.pdf</a></li><li>Safeguarding Resource and Support Hub (RSH): <a href="https://safeguardingsupporthub.org/">https://safeguardingsupporthub.org/</a></li><li>Information for grantseekers (Global Greengrants Fund): <a href="https://greengrants.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Info-for-Grantseekers_2023.pdf">https://greengrants.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Info-for-Grantseekers_2023.pdf</a></li></ul><p class="g">Prepared from the MazingiraKenya "Je, Hatua?" portfolio, 13 October 2026. Budgets are indicative planning figures, not quotes.</p></body></html>